    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "Custom events as dispatchers and handlers, the world broadcast, and engine event listeners.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 4/9: EVENT DISPATCHERS AND CUSTOM EVENTS\nA custom event (Events panel) has two halves: the red `On <name>` handler node and any number of\n`Call <name>` dispatch nodes. Fields are typed parameters. Three delivery paths are shown:\n 1) Dispatch node: a direct call inside this class.   2) Broadcast: the same event published to the\nworld as `AdvEventDispatchers.score_changed`, so OTHER classes can listen.\n 3) Engine events (GameBegan): the engine calls us. Declared event fields can be bool, integers, floats, String or Entity.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -290
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          190
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. LISTEN TO THE ENGINE - `On GameBegan` fires when play starts. It is an engine event with a `level`\noutput. We answer with two calls of our own `add_score` event (40 then 75 points).",
        "position": [
          -40,
          -80
        ],
        "size": [
          1020,
          270
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "gb",
          "gb_a1",
          "gb_a2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. THE SOURCE - `add_score(points)` updates the total, then DISPATCHES `score_changed(total, delta)`\nwith the fresh total (note the data wire from the Set node's output pin) and checks whether a\nnew hundred was crossed (score / 100 higher than `milestone_level`); if so it dispatches\n`milestone_reached(level)`. The producer knows nothing about who listens.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          390
        ],
        "size": [
          3040,
          710
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "as",
          "as_g",
          "as_add",
          "as_set",
          "as_chg",
          "as_lvl",
          "as_last",
          "as_higher",
          "as_if",
          "as_set_last",
          "as_ms"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. A HANDLER THAT PUBLISHES - the `On score_changed` handler logs, then BROADCASTS the same event to the\nworld (`Broadcast AdvEventDispatchers.score_changed`). Other objects subscribe with\n`On AdvEventDispatchers.score_changed` (scope global). A HUD class would do exactly that to\nshow the score. `Send ... to` targets one object instead; `Send ... to Class` all instances of a class.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          1310
        ],
        "size": [
          1340,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "sc",
          "sc_cat",
          "sc_log",
          "sc_bcast"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-5",
        "text": "4. A SIMPLE LISTENER - a milestone is rare, so it just logs. Real games would unlock a door, play\na fanfare or spawn a reward here. Integers are converted to text automatically when wired into a\nString pin.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          2000
        ],
        "size": [
          1000,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.8,
          0.3,
          0.3,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "ms_on",
          "ms_cat",
          "ms_log"
        ]
      }
    ],
